/-!
# `CatCryptDialect` → Veir op/type wiring

This file provides the `ToVeirOp catCryptDialect _` and
`ToVeirTy catCryptDialect` instances that let the generic `ComToVeir`
lowering (`lowerClosedCom`, `lowerClosedComToModuleWithExterns`, built by
`lowerComWfWith` in `ComToVeir.lean`) target real CatCrypt programs.

## Dependency

The instances require a Veir revision in which the lemma in
`Veir/ForLean.lean` is named `List.getElem_idxOf`, so that it does not collide
with `List.getElem?_idxOf` from Lean Init / Mathlib. The lakefile pins Veir at
`main`, which has that name.

## Goal 1: CatCrypt op inventory

Constructors of `CatCryptOp` (from `CatCryptDialect.lean`) and their
signatures, with the chosen Veir target op-code:

| Constructor              | Args                   | Result      | Veir target              |
|--------------------------|------------------------|-------------|--------------------------|
| `constBit b`             | none                   | `bit`       | `llvm_constant`          |
| `constUnit`              | none                   | `unit`      | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `xor`/`and`/`or`         | `bit, bit`             | `bit`       | `llvm_xor`/`and`/`or`    |
| `not`                    | `bit`                  | `bit`       | `arith_xori`             |
| `eqBit`                  | `bit, bit`             | `bit`       | `llvm_icmp`              |
| `mkPair a b`             | `a, b`                 | `pair a b`  | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `fst a b`                | `pair a b`             | `a`         | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `snd a b`                | `pair a b`             | `b`         | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `inl a b`                | `a`                    | `sum a b`   | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `inr a b`                | `b`                    | `sum a b`   | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `bvConst w v`            | none                   | `sword w`   | `llvm_constant`          |
| `bvXor w`/`And`/`Or`     | `sword w, sword w`     | `sword w`   | `llvm_xor`/`and`/`or`    |
| `bvNot w`                | `sword w`              | `sword w`   | `arith_xori`             |
| `bvAdd w`/`Sub w`/`Mul w`| `sword w, sword w`     | `sword w`   | `llvm_add`/`sub`/`mul`   |
| `bvEq w`                 | `sword w, sword w`     | `bit`       | `llvm_icmp`              |
| `bvShiftL w k`           | `sword w`              | `sword w`   | `llvm_shl`               |
| `bvShiftR w k`           | `sword w`              | `sword w`   | `llvm_lshr`              |
| `ite t`                  | `bit, t, t`            | `t`         | `arith_select`           |
| `bitToSword n`           | `bit`                  | `sword n`   | `llvm_sext`              |
| `memrefZero n`           | none                   | `memref n`  | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `memrefSet n i`          | `memref n, sword 64`   | `memref n`  | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `memrefGet n i`          | `memref n`             | `sword 64`  | `builtin_unregistered`   |
| `extCall …`              | varies                 | varies      | `builtin_unregistered`   |

Type mapping (`CryptoTy → Veir.TypeAttr`):

| CryptoTy   | TypeAttr                                  |
|------------|-------------------------------------------|
| `bit`      | `IntegerType.signless 1`                  |
| `unit`     | `default` (== `IntegerType.signless 0`)   |
| `sword n`  | `IntegerType.signless n`                  |
| `pair _ _` | `default` (no Veir pair type)             |
| `sum _ _`  | `default` (structural placeholder)  |
| `memref _` | `default` (structural placeholder)  |

Notes on the op mapping:

* `bitToSword n` ("if c then allOnes else 0") is the sign extension
  `i1 → iN`: `llvm_sext` here, `arith_extsi` in `toArithOpCode`.
* Pair / sum / memref ops have no single Veir operation with their
  denotation, so they lower to `catcrypt.unknown`, an unregistered op that
  MLIR accepts under `--allow-unregistered-dialect`, with operands and results
  in place and no semantics.

## Goal 2: Veir op-code mechanism

`Veir.OpCode` is an enum generated by `#generate_op_codes` with one
constructor per dialect, each taking that dialect's `@[opcodes]` inductive
from `Veir/Dialects/<Dialect>/OpInfo.lean`, e.g. `.arith .addi`,
`.llvm .xor`.

* **Properties** per op-code are given by `Veir.propertiesOf`, the
  `IsOpCode` family assembled in `Veir/GlobalOpInfo.lean` from the
  per-dialect `propertiesOf` matches. The result is either a specific
  property structure (`ArithConstantProperties`, `FuncCallProperties`, …)
  or `Unit` for ops without properties. All property structures are
  `Inhabited`, so `default` always produces a value.
* **Unregistered fallback**: `OpCode.builtin .unregistered` is the
  tag of an op from a dialect Veir does not register; its properties
  carry the operation name, which the printer emits.
* **No per-user extension**: there is no `registerOpCode` mechanism;
  the enum is fixed at Veir build-time. CatCrypt-native op-codes live in
  the `@[opcodes] inductive Catcrypt` of
  `Veir/Dialects/Catcrypt/OpInfo.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR

open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.CatCryptDialect
open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.CryptoSSA
open CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR.LatticeDialect (LatticeOp)

-- The upstream `HasOpInfo Veir.OpCode` instance from `Veir.GlobalOpInfo`
-- provides per-op-code property types (`ArithConstantProperties`,
-- `FuncCallProperties`, …) and is the one expected by
-- `Veir.Printer.printModule`. We inherit it directly via `inferInstance`
-- in the `ToVeirOp` instance below, rather than defining a local
-- `Unit`-everywhere variant; this means `defaultProps` has to supply
-- the correct property type for each op-code our `toOp` produces. All
-- property types are `Inhabited`, so `default` always works.

/-- Map each `CatCryptOp` constructor to a Veir `OpCode`.

    Ops with no direct Veir counterpart (pair/sum/memref construction,
    `constUnit`) route to `catcrypt.unknown` — a local Veir dialect
    extension whose only purpose is to give MLIR a non-`builtin`
    prefix it can accept under `--allow-unregistered-dialect`. -/
def CatCryptOp.toVeirOp : CatCryptOp → Veir.OpCode
  | .constBit _ => .llvm .mlir__constant
  | .constUnit => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .xor => .llvm .xor
  | .and => .llvm .and
  | .or => .llvm .or
  | .not => .arith .xori
  | .eqBit => .llvm .icmp
  | .mkPair _ _ | .fst _ _ | .snd _ _ | .inl _ _ | .inr _ _ =>
      .catcrypt .unknown
  | .bvConst _ _ => .llvm .mlir__constant
  | .bvXor _ => .llvm .xor
  | .bvAnd _ => .llvm .and
  | .bvOr _ => .llvm .or
  | .bvNot _ => .arith .xori
  | .bvAdd _ => .llvm .add
  | .bvSub _ => .llvm .sub
  | .bvMul _ => .llvm .mul
  | .bvEq _ => .llvm .icmp
  | .bvShiftL _ _ => .llvm .shl
  | .bvShiftR _ _ => .llvm .lshr
  -- Variable-amount logical shifts (shift count read from a register operand).
  | .bvShiftLV _ => .llvm .shl
  | .bvShiftRV _ => .llvm .lshr
  -- Word-native crypto ops with no single Veir opcode (rotates, sign-shift,
  -- andn) route to the unregistered escape (lowered later to `llvm.fshr`/etc).
  | .bvRor _ _ | .bvRol _ _ | .bvShiftRA _ _ | .andn _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  -- Multi-output add-with-carry: no single Veir opcode produces both the
  -- carry-out and sum, so route to the unregistered escape (as with sampling).
  | .bvAdd64 _ | .bvAdc _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  -- Bignum ALU word splits: no single Veir opcode, unregistered escape.
  | .bvMulHi _ | .bvAddCarryLo _ | .bvAddCarryHi _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .ite _ => .arith .select
  | .bitToSword _ => .llvm .sext
  | .memrefZero _ | .memrefSet _ _ | .memrefGet _ _
  | .memrefSetDyn _ | .memrefGetDyn _ | .memrefGetDyn128 _
  | .memrefWSetDyn _ _ | .memrefWGetDyn _ _ =>
      .catcrypt .unknown
  | .extCall _ _ _ => .func .call
  | .sampleBit | .sampleBv _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  -- 128-bit SIMD ops: no single registered Veir opcode, unregistered escape.
  | .vsimd _ | .vpshufdC _ | .vaeskeygenC _ | .vpsrldqC _ | .vpslldqC _
  | .vconst128 _
  | .vsha256rnds2 | .vsha256msg1 | .vsha256msg2 =>
      .catcrypt .unknown

/-- **MLIR `arith`-dialect lowering pass.** Maps each `CatCryptOp` whose
    denotation is that of one registered MLIR operation over the binding's
    operands to that operation's opcode in the `arith`, `memref` or `func`
    dialect; every other op maps to `catcrypt.unknown`.

    * `bvMulHi w` is `arith.mului_extended`, whose second result
      (`resultSlotOfOp`) is the high word.
    * `bitToSword n` is `arith.extsi` (`c ↦ allOnes` or `0`).
    * `bvShiftLV`, `bvShiftRV` are `arith.shli`, `arith.shrui`: equal to the
      denotation for an amount `< w`, where MLIR yields poison and the
      denotation `0`. The instance `ToVeirOp catCryptDialect` lowers them through
      `CatCryptOp.shiftSelectExpansion`, which selects `0` for an amount `≥ w`.
    * `not`, `bvNot`, the immediate shifts, rotates and `andn` need a constant
      operand, `bvAddCarryLo/Hi`, `bvAdd64`, `bvAdc` a chain of operations, the
      memref reads an `index` operand reduced modulo `n`, and the memref updates
      a fresh buffer; one registered operation does not express them, so they
      map to `catcrypt.unknown`. The text printer `CatCryptPrint` renders all of
      them as sequences of upstream operations. -/
def CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode : CatCryptOp → Veir.OpCode
  | .constBit _ => .arith .constant
  | .constUnit => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .xor => .arith .xori
  | .and => .arith .andi
  | .or => .arith .ori
  | .not => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .eqBit => .arith .cmpi
  | .mkPair _ _ | .fst _ _ | .snd _ _ | .inl _ _ | .inr _ _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .bvConst _ _ => .arith .constant
  | .bvXor _ => .arith .xori
  | .bvAnd _ => .arith .andi
  | .bvOr _ => .arith .ori
  | .bvNot _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .bvAdd _ => .arith .addi
  | .bvSub _ => .arith .subi
  | .bvMul _ => .arith .muli
  | .bvEq _ => .arith .cmpi
  | .bvShiftL _ _ | .bvShiftR _ _ | .bvShiftRA _ _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  -- Variable-amount logical shifts: equal to the denotation for an amount `< w`.
  | .bvShiftLV _ => .arith .shli
  | .bvShiftRV _ => .arith .shrui
  | .bvRor _ _ | .bvRol _ _ | .andn _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .bvAdd64 _ | .bvAdc _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .bvMulHi _ => .arith .mului_extended
  | .bvAddCarryLo _ | .bvAddCarryHi _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .ite _ => .arith .select
  | .bitToSword _ => .arith .extsi
  | .memrefZero _ | .memrefGet _ _ | .memrefGetDyn128 _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .memrefGetDyn _ | .memrefWGetDyn _ _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .memrefSet _ _ | .memrefSetDyn _ | .memrefWSetDyn _ _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  | .extCall _ _ _ => .func .call
  | .sampleBit | .sampleBv _ => .catcrypt .unknown
  -- 128-bit SIMD ops: no registered `arith`/`memref` opcode, unregistered escape.
  | .vsimd _ | .vpshufdC _ | .vaeskeygenC _ | .vpsrldqC _ | .vpslldqC _
  | .vconst128 _
  | .vsha256rnds2 | .vsha256msg1 | .vsha256msg2 =>
      .catcrypt .unknown

/-! Instances of the `arith`-lowering map, checked by `rfl`. -/
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvAdd 32) = .arith .addi := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvSub 32) = .arith .subi := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvMul 16) = .arith .muli := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvXor 64) = .arith .xori := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvShiftLV 32) = .arith .shli := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvShiftRV 32) = .arith .shrui := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvEq 16) = .arith .cmpi := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.ite (.sword 64)) = .arith .select := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bitToSword 64) = .arith .extsi := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.bvMulHi 64) = .arith .mului_extended := rfl
example : CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode (.extCall "fp_mul" [] (.sword 64)) = .func .call := rfl

/-- **MLIR `polynomial`-dialect lowering pass** for the `latticeDialect` (the
    ML-KEM/Dilithium NTT layer). Maps each `LatticeOp` to a REGISTERED MLIR
    `polynomial.*` opcode (Veir's new `Polynomial` block) — the upstream dialect
    for `Z_q[X]/(f)` arithmetic — instead of treating the NTT ops as opaque
    `func.call` leaves. `basemul` (NTT-domain) and `polyMulC` (coefficient) both
    lower to `polynomial.mul` (the ring is the dialect's ring attribute). -/
def LatticeOp.toPolynomialOpCode : LatticeOp → Veir.OpCode
  | .ntt _ _ => .polynomial .ntt
  | .invntt _ _ => .polynomial .intt
  | .basemul _ _ => .polynomial .mul
  | .polyAddN _ _ => .polynomial .add
  | .polyMulC _ _ => .polynomial .mul

example : LatticeOp.toPolynomialOpCode (.ntt 3329 256) = .polynomial .ntt := rfl
example : LatticeOp.toPolynomialOpCode (.invntt 3329 256) = .polynomial .intt := rfl
example : LatticeOp.toPolynomialOpCode (.basemul 3329 256) = .polynomial .mul := rfl
example : LatticeOp.toPolynomialOpCode (.polyAddN 3329 256) = .polynomial .add := rfl

/-- The results of an op's Veir operation: `bvMulHi` is `arith.mului_extended`,
    whose two results are the low and the high word, the high word being the value;
    every other op has one result. -/
def CatCryptOp.resultSlotOfOp : CatCryptOp → Nat × Nat
  | .bvMulHi _ => (2, 1)
  | _ => (1, 0)

/-- The properties of an op's Veir operation: the value of an `arith.constant`
    (`bvConst`, `constBit`), the callee `@name` of the `func.call` of
    `extCall name`, the `eq` predicate of the `arith.cmpi` of `eqBit` and `bvEq`,
    and the default properties otherwise. -/
def CatCryptOp.propsOfOp (o : CatCryptOp) :
    Veir.propertiesOf (CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode o) :=
  match o with
  | .bvConst w v =>
      ({ value := ⟨v.toNat, Veir.IntegerType.signless w⟩ } : Veir.ArithConstantProperties)
  | .constBit b =>
      ({ value := ⟨if b then 1 else 0, Veir.IntegerType.signless 1⟩ } :
        Veir.ArithConstantProperties)
  | .extCall name _ _ => VeirPrinterShim.funcCallProps name
  | .eqBit => ({ predicate := .eq } : Veir.IcmpProperties)
  | .bvEq _ => ({ predicate := .eq } : Veir.IcmpProperties)
  | _ => default

/-- The lowering of a variable-amount shift of `w`-bit words by the `arith` op
    `shiftOp` (`shli` or `shrui`) as five operations: the constant `w`,
    `arith.cmpi uge` of the amount (argument 1) against it, the shift of argument 0
    by argument 1, the constant `0`, and `arith.select` of `0` when the amount is at
    least `w` and of the shift otherwise. The value is the result of the
    `arith.select`. `arith.shli` and `arith.shrui` are poison for an amount at least
    the width, and `arith.select` does not propagate poison from the arm it does not
    pick. -/
def CatCryptOp.shiftSelectExpansion (shiftOp : Veir.Arith) (w : Nat) :
    VeirExpansion Veir.OpCode where
  steps :=
    [ { op := .arith .constant,
        props := ({ value := ⟨(BitVec.ofNat w w).toNat, Veir.IntegerType.signless w⟩ } :
          Veir.ArithConstantProperties),
        operands := [], results := [none] },
      { op := .arith .cmpi, props := ({ predicate := .uge } : Veir.IcmpProperties),
        operands := [.arg 1, .res 0 0],
        results := [some ((Veir.IntegerType.signless 1 : Veir.IntegerType) : Veir.TypeAttr)] },
      { op := .arith shiftOp, props := default,
        operands := [.arg 0, .arg 1], results := [none] },
      { op := .arith .constant,
        props := ({ value := ⟨0, Veir.IntegerType.signless w⟩ } : Veir.ArithConstantProperties),
        operands := [], results := [none] },
      { op := .arith .select, props := default,
        operands := [.res 1 0, .res 3 0, .res 2 0], results := [none] } ]
  value := .res 4 0

/-- The ops of `catCryptDialect` that lower to more than one operation: the
    variable-amount shifts `bvShiftLV w` and `bvShiftRV w`, as
    `shiftSelectExpansion`. -/
def CatCryptOp.expandVeir? : CatCryptOp → Option (VeirExpansion Veir.OpCode)
  | .bvShiftLV w => some (CatCryptOp.shiftSelectExpansion .shli w)
  | .bvShiftRV w => some (CatCryptOp.shiftSelectExpansion .shrui w)
  | _ => none

instance : ToVeirOp catCryptDialect where
  Op := Veir.OpCode
  hasOpInfo := inferInstance
  -- Lower to the registered MLIR `arith`/`func` mid-level dialect (upstream-pass
  -- compatible), not the LLVM-dialect forms in the legacy `toVeirOp`.
  toOp := CatCryptOp.toArithOpCode
  defaultProps := CatCryptOp.propsOfOp
  resultSlot := CatCryptOp.resultSlotOfOp
  expand? := CatCryptOp.expandVeir?

/-- Build an `UnregisteredAttr` carrying MLIR-textual type syntax for
    structural types that have no native Veir `TypeAttr` (memref,
    pair, sum). The string is emitted verbatim by Veir's printer. -/
def mkTextType (s : String) : Veir.TypeAttr :=
  ⟨.unregisteredAttr { value := s, isType := true }, by simp [Veir.Attribute.isType]⟩

/-- Map each `CryptoTy` to a Veir `TypeAttr`.

    * `sword n` and `bit` use Veir's native `IntegerType`.
    * `memref n` is "n × i64" per `CryptoTy.denote` (`Fin n → BitVec 64`),
      so it prints as `memref<n×i64>`.
    * `pair`/`sum` are recursive structural; we recurse into the
      operands and emit MLIR-style tuple text (`tuple<a, b>`,
      `tuple<sum, a, b>`).
    * `unit` is the empty tuple. -/
def CryptoTy.toVeirTy : CryptoTy → Veir.TypeAttr
  | .bit => (Veir.IntegerType.signless 1 : Veir.IntegerType)
  | .unit => mkTextType "tuple<>"
  | .sword n => (Veir.IntegerType.signless n : Veir.IntegerType)
  | .pair a b =>
      mkTextType s!"tuple<{toVeirTy a}, {toVeirTy b}>"
  | .sum a b =>
      mkTextType s!"tuple<sum, {toVeirTy a}, {toVeirTy b}>"
  | .memref n => mkTextType s!"memref<{n}xi64>"
  | .memrefW w n => mkTextType s!"memref<{n}xi{w}>"

instance : ToVeirTy catCryptDialect where
  toTy := CryptoTy.toVeirTy

/-! ## Extern collection (for module-with-externs emission) -/

/-- Externs referenced by a single `CatCryptOp`. Today only
    `CatCryptOp.extCall` contributes; everything else returns `[]`. -/
def CatCryptOp.externOfOp :
    (op : CatCryptOp) → List (String × List CryptoTy × CryptoTy)
  | .extCall name argTys retTy => [(name, argTys, retTy)]
  | _ => []

/-- All externs referenced by `Com`, in source order, with duplicates.
    Caller can dedup. -/
def Com.catcryptExterns :
    {Γ : Ctxt catCryptDialect} → {t : CryptoTy} →
      Com catCryptDialect Γ t →
      List (String × List CryptoTy × CryptoTy)
  | _, _, .ret _ => []
  | _, _, .var e body =>
      CatCryptOp.externOfOp e.op ++ Com.catcryptExterns body

/-- Dedup externs by callee name (first occurrence wins). Stable. -/
def dedupExternsByName :
    List (String × List CryptoTy × CryptoTy) →
      List (String × List CryptoTy × CryptoTy)
  | [] => []
  | x :: rest =>
      let restDedup := dedupExternsByName rest
      if restDedup.any (fun y => y.1 = x.1) then restDedup
      else x :: restDedup

/-! ## Smoke test

A tiny `Com` over `CatCryptDialect` (a single `bvAdd 32`) is lowered
via the generic `lowerClosedCom`. The type-check itself is the smoke
signal — Veir's `HashMap`-backed `IRContext` doesn't reduce via Lean's
kernel for `decide`. -/

namespace SmokeTestCatCrypt

open CatCryptDialect

/-- A one-`var` `Com` over `CatCryptDialect`: bind a `bvConst 32 0` and
    return its result. We deliberately use a constant rather than a
    binary op so the smoke test stays closed (no free variables for
    operands).

    Note: the existing nullary `Expr.mk` shape (`args := .nil`) matches
    a `DialectSignature.sig` that returns `[]`, so we need a nullary
    op — `bvConst 32 0` qualifies. -/
def exampleCom : Com catCryptDialect [] (CryptoTy.sword 32) :=
  .var (Expr.mk (op := CatCryptOp.bvConst 32 (0 : BitVec 32))
                (retTy_eq := rfl) (args := .nil))
       (.ret .here)

/-- Smoke test: the lowering type-checks end-to-end and produces a
    concrete `IRContext × BlockPtr × RegionPtr × ValuePtr` value. -/
example : Veir.IRContext Veir.OpCode × Veir.BlockPtr × Veir.RegionPtr ×
    Veir.ValuePtr :=
  lowerClosedCom (d := catCryptDialect) exampleCom

/-- End-to-end pipeline: lower a closed `Com` over `CatCryptDialect`
    through `lowerClosedCom` (Veir IRContext), then through the
    `VeirPrinterShim.printModuleToString` to capture MLIR text.

    For a printable module use `lowerClosedComToModuleWithExterns`
    (as `X25519EmitVeir.emitFuncToVeirText` does). This helper extracts the producing op pointer from the
    final `ValuePtr` purely for the legacy smoke test below. -/
def lowerCatCryptComToMLIRText {t : CryptoTy} (com : Com catCryptDialect [] t) :
    IO String := do
  let (ctx, _blk, _reg, finalResult) :=
    lowerClosedCom (d := catCryptDialect) com
  let rootOp : Veir.OperationPtr :=
    match finalResult with
    | .opResult r => r.op
    | .blockArgument _ => default
  VeirPrinterShim.printModuleToString ctx rootOp

/-- Smoke check that the printer wiring type-checks. It is not
    evaluated: running Veir's printer against the lowered shape is outside
    this check. -/
example : Com catCryptDialect [] (CryptoTy.sword 32) → IO String :=
  lowerCatCryptComToMLIRText

end SmokeTestCatCrypt

end CatCrypt.Crypto.SecureCompilation.VIR
